    "Transcript_Log": "Agent: Good evening, thank you for calling Duroflex.\nCustomer: Bhaiya, was I just talking to you?\nAgent: You were talking to Kunal ji, please tell me.\nCustomer: I am asking, what is the difference in material between Balance and Balance Plus?\nAgent: Sir, Balance Plus has an additional layer of memory foam, that's the only difference, and it's 8 inches thick. And it has a Euro top finish.\nCustomer: And the zone support, that's also in it?\nAgent: Everything is there, sir, in that too.\nCustomer: Memory foam and Euro top, just these two differences?\nAgent: Yes, sir.\nCustomer: Okay. And are there any other models in 8 inches?\nAgent: In 8 inches, we also have a Posture Perfect, which has pocket springs in the base with heat away technology. It has graphite. It's more expensive.\nCustomer: Yes, it will cost you approximately 65,000. With that, you will get a one-seater recliner complimentary.\nCustomer: In Balance and this, the only difference is memory foam and Euro top?\nAgent: Euro top is the difference.\nCustomer: What is Euro top?\nAgent: It's a layer that is made like that. Additional in plus. What difference does it make?\nCustomer: It's a bit like a design, it looks a bit better and enhanced.\nCustomer: And what is the thickness of the memory foam?\nAgent: 2 inches thickness. If we talk about the total, we count it as 6 plus 2. The base is 6 inches and the layer above is 2 inches, total.\nCustomer: So, the difference is 1 inch, what else is there?\nAgent: Yes, sir.\nCustomer: Balance and Overall, if we talk about it, there is a difference of 1 inch in height.\nCustomer: So, what material is less in it? What has increased by 1 inch?\nAgent: Nothing, just the layer has increased. Proportionately, as I am telling you, like we have an 8-inch mattress, we don't count the height of the quilt. I am saying, in Balance, if this 2-inch memory foam is minus, then 6 is left, so what is the 7 in it?\nAgent: See, total overall, I am talking about the height, so it comes to around 8.5 inches, our Balance Plus.\nCustomer: Okay. So, the only difference is the top layer.\nCustomer: So, the top layer is 2 inches in it? We count approximately, it's not exact, it's approximate.\nCustomer: If we remove this top layer, then the bonded, bonded, whatever foam will be, is it all equal in both?\nAgent: It's equal, both are equal.\nCustomer: Okay. Everything is equal. Below you will get bonded, above that, 5 zone orthopedic layer. And in Balance, you only get memory foam quilting on top. And in this, you get an additional layer.\nCustomer: You are denying that there is memory foam in Balance?\nAgent: No, no, no, it's there in that too, sir.\nCustomer: What is not there in it?\nAgent: No, Balance Plus has memory foam, sir. Both have it.\nCustomer: No, in Balance?\nAgent: In Balance, it is used only in the quilt. The fabric that is stitched with the top layer, it is only used in that. In Balance Plus, a separate layer is put and then the quilt is put.\nCustomer: Okay. Okay, okay. Okay, okay. I will send you photos of both, you can see from that.\nCustomer: Send it, send it, man.\nAgent: Okay. Okay."
}

